  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zea Municipality Flood Emergency Relief</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide support in several inter-related aspects that have an overall positive impact for the affected population: WASH items (detailed below) will help prevent the spread of waterborne diseases as well as skin diseases due to lack of proper hygiene and water sources contamination and will help prevent the spread of COVID-19; primary health services (medical consultation plus medication) will help to treat acute diseases related to poor hygiene (parasites, skin infections, etc) and aid in the control of chronic non-communicable diseases, both of which can lead to complications that can cause limited functionality and dependence; food item provision to help reduce the risk of malnutrition, anemia and other health conditions that can have serious consequences for the health of the affected population. All these areas of intervention will improve the quality of life and living standards of a population with critical needs for mutliple forms of assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">all assistance can be provided to all 3,300 targeted beneficiaries within 45-day implementation period, potential difficulties arising from two main Countire&apos;s contextual factors need to be considered and managed: eventual military intervention, and</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">the assisted families will have improved access to food, health and WASH thus reducing their risk of morbidity, extreme hunger, thirst and health risks. It will increase their capacity and resources to prevent communicable diseases (water and food related) including COVID-19, have better access to the means to control non-communicable diseases, and can reduce the negative effects of natural disasters on their livelihoods and life conditions. The assistance provided will have a positive impact in their psycho-social wellbeing and quality of life, helping them in their recovery efforts and promoting quality of life and dignity after a natural disaster.</narrative>
  </description>
